       "transcription": {
        "@type": "text",
        "@id": "copies/vm096df0179#inscription-text",
        "text": "№ 363.  7. 1108.  Roth",
        "@annotation": {
         "@id": "copies/vm096df0179#transcription-annotation",
         "belief": {
          "@type": "belief",
          "@id": "copies/vm096df0179#transcription-belief",
          "certainty": "likely",
          "reasons": [
           {
            "@type": "meaningComprehension",
            "comprehends": [
             "copies/vm096df0179#inscription"
            ],
            "note": "Graded medium on the figures of the date: one figure is arguable. Faint pencil. '№ 363.' and 'Roth' are clear. The four figures after the day read 1-1-0-8, i.e. month 11 and year 08 with the separators dropped; if the second figure were a 9 the group would be the year '1908' and the inscription would carry no month. The day is written with a flat top bar and could be a 1 rather than a 7."
           }
          ]
         }
        }
       }
      }
     ],
